PHASE 1 - FOUNDATION.

1. Scaffold Next.js App Router + TypeScript (strict) + Tailwind. Three environments: development, preview, production, each with its own Supabase project and its own Paystack keys (test keys everywhere except production). Provide .env.example with variable names only.

2. Migrations (committed, repeatable): profiles (id = auth.users.id, role enum 'owner'|'staff'|'developer', is_active boolean, full_name), business_settings (single row, key/value json, updated_by), audit_logs (id, actor_id, actor_role, action, entity, entity_id, before jsonb, after jsonb, ip_hash, created_at).

3. audit_logs MUST be append-only: revoke UPDATE and DELETE from every role and add a trigger that raises on update/delete. Write a test that proves an UPDATE fails.

4. Auth: Supabase Auth email + password. Owner and developer accounts require MFA. Revoked (is_active=false) accounts lose access on the next request. Customers do NOT need accounts (guest checkout).

5. Authorization: one server-side helper requireRole(['owner']) used by every protected action. Row Level Security enabled on every table with least-privilege policies. Staff cannot change roles, settings or prices.

6. Money module (lib/money.ts) with unit tests: formatNaira(kobo: bigint): string, parseNairaToKobo(input: string): bigint, applyPercentRoundHalfUp(kobo, bps), MAX_KOBO constant. Use integer math only.

