PHASE 2 - EDITABLE MENU. Phase 1 is complete and merged.

Build the menu data model exactly as in the playbook schema (migrations + RLS), then:

A. OWNER MENU EDITOR (dashboard, mobile-first, usable one-handed):
   - List grouped by category with search and filters (published / draft / archived / sold out).
   - Item form: name, description, category, price typed in naira and converted with parseNairaToKobo ON THE SERVER (never trust a client-converted number), portion label, allergens, photo, alt text, featured, option groups and options with price deltas.
   - One-tap 'Sold out today' and 'Available' toggles on the list itself.
   - Up/down reorder buttons for items and categories.
   - Price-change confirmation dialog showing old and new values in ₦.
   - Version history per item with one-tap restore.
   - Archive instead of delete. Block hard delete when any order_items or invoice line references the item.
   - Optimistic locking using the version column.
   - Every save writes menu_item_versions and audit_logs.

B. IMAGE UPLOAD: accept JPEG/PNG/WebP up to 5 MB, verify magic bytes (not just the extension), strip EXIF, generate 400/800/1600 px WebP, store in a public bucket with random file names. Reject everything else with a clear message. If an item has no photo, show a neutral 'Photo coming soon' tile. Never use stock or AI-generated food images.

C. CSV IMPORT/EXPORT: export the full menu. Import with a mandatory DRY-RUN step that shows: rows to create, rows to update (old to new price), rows rejected and why. Nothing is written until the owner presses Confirm. Match on sku (or category+name). Reject duplicate names in a category, prices that parse to more than MAX_KOBO, prices under 1 kobo, blank names, unknown categories (offer to create). The commit is one database transaction: all rows or none. Importing the same file twice must change nothing the second time (idempotent). Cap at 500 rows.

D. PUBLIC MENU: server-rendered, shows only published items in visible categories, hides empty categories, shows unavailable and sold-out items greyed with 'Sold out today' (per decision 3) and disables add-to-cart. Revalidate the public pages immediately on any menu change. Include a complete empty-menu state and a failed-load state.

E. PRICE SAFETY: expose a server function getOrderablePrice(itemId, optionIds) that is the ONLY source of prices for later phases. Add a database check that raises if any published item has price 0 unless the owner flags it as 'free item'.

F. TESTS: unit and integration tests for every rule above, using the golden menu fixture in the playbook section 14. Show me output.

Do not build the cart or checkout yet.
Owner cheat sheet (give this to whoever edits the menu)
1. Change a price: open the item, type the new ₦ amount, confirm the old to new screen.
2. Dish finished for the day: tap 'Sold out today'. It resets itself at midnight.
3. New dish: add it as draft, add a photo and alt text, then press Publish.
4. Wrong edit: open Version history and tap Restore.
5. Many prices at once: export the CSV, edit it, import it, and read the dry-run before confirming.
