CART: client-side for display only. The client sends ONLY item ids, option ids and quantities. The server loads prices from the database through getOrderablePrice, recomputes everything, and ignores any price, total or fee sent by the browser.

CHECKOUT VALIDATION: quantity 1-50 per line (configurable); total above a configurable ceiling goes to 'needs review'; unavailable, archived, sold-out or draft items are rejected with the item named; phone normalized to +234 E.164 (accept 080..., 234..., +234...); address required for delivery; requested time must be in the future; delivery zone must be active or the order is flagged 'manual delivery review'; honeypot field; rate limit per IP and per phone; idempotency key so a double tap creates ONE order; same phone + same items within 2 minutes returns the existing order instead of creating a second.

CAPACITY AND CUT-OFF: read max_orders_per_day and cut-off from business_settings. When a day is full, show 'We are fully booked for that date' and offer other dates. Defaults are 'unlimited' until the owner sets them.

AFTER SUBMIT: status 'awaiting_confirmation'. Show a confirmation page at /order/<public_token> that says plainly: 'Request received. It is NOT confirmed until our team confirms it.' A prefilled WhatsApp link is OPTIONAL and must be described as a shortcut, not as proof of sending. Guest status page shows status and items only, no other customer data.

ALERTS (mandatory): on every new order create an in-dashboard alert with a sound, and send an email to the configured recipients. Include ref, total in ₦, fulfilment type and requested time. Log delivery failures. Provide a 'needs attention' list for any order awaiting confirmation longer than the configured threshold.

EXPIRY: a scheduled job (database cron or scheduled function) marks unconfirmed orders 'expired' after the configured window, tells the customer by the channel they gave, and writes an order_event. A stale guest link shows a clear 'expired' state.

STATES: loading, empty cart, closed day, item went unavailable mid-checkout, network failure on submit (safe to retry), expired order, unknown token (generic 404, no hint whether it exists).

TESTS using the golden fixtures: manipulated total rejected; price edited in the menu after ordering does not change the old order; sequential token guessing returns 404; double submit creates one order; full day blocks; expiry fires; alert row created.
Exit gate: twenty scripted test orders on a real phone, including a manipulated-total attempt, a double tap, a sold-out item and a full day. Your phone buzzes or the dashboard alerts within a minute of each. No order exists without a snapshot.
