21 PDF amounts that bleed out of their column: finding and fix (22 Oct 2026)
What I checked first. I exported this playbook to PDF (46 pages at that time) and measured it: 0 words outside a 36 point safety margin on every page, and 0 words crossing a table column line. The ₦ sign rendered correctly on every page I viewed (pages 12 and 45 among them). So the playbook PDF itself does not have the fault. If a different PDF is the one you saw, send me that file and the page number.
What I found in the project's own PDF code. The Money component placed the ₦ sign and the digits in nested text. In a narrow cell the renderer wrapped them onto two lines: the ₦ on its own line and the figure (for example 100,000,000.00) on the line below. That is the 'figure bleeding out' risk for the invoices and receipts to come. No invoice or receipt template existed in the repo at that point, so this was caught before any customer document used it. An invoice template was added afterwards (see section 22).
