21.3 How to check any PDF for figures bleeding out
# 1. Word positions (needs poppler):  pdftotext -bbox your.pdf -
# 2. Whole-document check against a 36 point safety margin (needs Python with pdfplumber):

import sys, pdfplumber
MARGIN = 36.0
with pdfplumber.open(sys.argv[1]) as pdf:
    for i, pg in enumerate(pdf.pages, 1):
        W = pg.width
        bad = [w['text'] for w in pg.extract_words() if w['x1'] > W - MARGIN + 0.5 or w['x0'] < MARGIN - 0.5]
        if bad: print('page', i, 'outside the margin:', bad[:8])

# 3. Look at the page: pdftoppm -f 12 -l 12 -r 80 -png your.pdf page
This check finds text beyond the margin and, with pdftotext -bbox, text that spills out of a table column. It cannot see a figure that a PDF viewer clips without moving, so also open a few pages by eye.
