28.5 Keep me signed in (added 8 Nov 2026, built and tested)
What it does. The team sign-in page has a box, Keep me signed in on this device, off by default, with the warning: Stays signed in for up to 30 days. Do not tick this on a shared or public phone. Customers never sign in and never see this box. The page still says: Customers do not need an account.
Why it is not just a longer session. The Supabase library, left alone, keeps the sign-in cookies for 400 days. That is too long for a phone that is lost or shared. Now the sign-in cookies have no expiry unless the box is ticked, so the browser forgets them when it closes. With the box ticked they last at most 30 days.
